codemap 9
tour feature-peek-definition
kind flow
author ai
group features/gui
note Alt-click an identifier in any code view to keep its definition at the top of the References view, above the xrefs, without leaving the place being read. The References view is brought into sight for it: its tab activated, or, when no panel holds it, a new panel split off to the right of the centre view. The reader reaches for it to check what an identifier is without losing their place in the step or file being read. The peek shows the symbol's whole text, or the lines around a definition that is not a symbol's start, or a definition outside the repo read from disk. Its 'go' button goes there (a symbol is focused, a line opens in the Source view; an outside definition has no go), and 'x' closes it. The peek stays until closed or replaced.

